summary:
  A widget on the desktop puts its face in a window because an old config key says so.

history:
  The desktop form shows the face inline and is offered no window: there
  the window cut six pixels off each side of the face. The key can still
  be set from the widget's days in a panel, and it must not be obeyed.

target:
  package/contents/ui/WindowLogic.js

find:
      return detached === true && planar !== true ? "window" : "popup";

replace:
      return detached === true ? "window" : "popup";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_windowlogic.qml::test_a_desktop_widget_keeps_its_face_whatever_the_config_says.
